**EXERCISE 7.18.** Two effectively given systems $D$ and $E$ are *effectively isomorphic* iff … (complete the sentence!). Show that if $D$ is effectively given then the isomorphism

$$D^\infty \cong (D^\infty)^\infty$$

is effective.

<!-- page 132 -->

The development is with the [effective isomorphism](1980_effectiveIso.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`example_718`).** An iterate is effectively isomorphic to the iterate of that iterate.

*Proof.* By the effective isomorphism. ∎
